thin the document.","The <a> element defines a hyperlink, and the href attribute specifies the URL of the page.","The alt attribute provides alternative text for images if they fail to load or for screen readers.","The input type=\"range\" defines a control for entering a number whose exact value is not important.","The <textarea> tag defines a multi-line text input control, often used for comments or feedback.","The GET method appends form data to the URL query string, making it visible and bookmarkable.","The <td> tag defines a standard data cell in an HTML table.","The colspan attribute defines the number of columns a table cell should span.","The <figure> tag specifies self-contained content, like illustrations, diagrams, photos, code listings, etc.","The <audio> element is used to embed sound content in HTML5 documents.","The <nav> tag defines a set of navigation links.","CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets. It is used to format the layout of a webpage.","The <style> tag is used to define internal CSS rules in the head section of an HTML document.","The ''''#'''' symbol targets an element with a specific id in CSS.","The :hover pseudo-class matches when the user designates an element with a pointing device.","Padding is the space between the content of an element and its border.","Margin is the outermost layer of the box model, separating the element from other elements.","position: absolute positions an element relative to its nearest positioned ancestor."]',
  'published'
);

