 it relative to its closest positioned ancestor?","a":"relative","b":"absolute","c":"static","d":"fixed"},{"q":"Which CSS display value enables a flex container? (Study Guide Question)","a":"display: grid;","b":"display: flex;","c":"display: block-flex;","d":"display: inline-grid;"},{"q":"Which flexbox property defines the alignment of items along the main axis?","a":"align-items","b":"align-content","c":"justify-content","d":"flex-direction"},{"q":"Which CSS property specifies the column gap size in a Grid layout?","a":"grid-column-gap","b":"column-gap","c":"gap-columns","d":"grid-gap-width"},{"q":"What is the primary CSS rule used to apply responsive styles based on screen width?","a":"@media","b":"@import","c":"@responsive","d":"@keyframes"},{"q":"Which Bootstrap class is used to create a responsive container?","a":".container","b":".row","c":".col-md-12","d":".grid-responsive"},{"q":"Inside which HTML element do we put JavaScript? (Study Guide Question)","a":"<js>","b":"<scripting>","c":"<script>","d":"<javascript>"},{"q":"Which keyword is used to declare a block-scoped variable in ES6?","a":"var","b":"let","c":"define","d":"set"},{"q":"How do you write a function in JavaScript?","a":"function myFunction()","b":"function:myFunction()","c":"def myFunction()","d":"create myFunction()"},{"q":"How do you call a function named ''myFunction''?","a":"call myFunction()","b":"myFunction()","c":"execute myFunction","d":"run myFunction"},{"q":"Which method adds a new element to the end of a JavaScript array?","a":"push()","b":"pop()","c":"shift()","d":"unshift()"},{"q":"How does a ''for'' loop start in JavaScript? (Study Guide Question)","a":"for (i = 0; i <= 5)","b":"for (i <= 5; i++)","c":"for (let i = 0; i <= 5; i++)","d":"for i = 1 to 5"},{"q":"Which method is used to select an element by its unique ID in the DOM?","a":"document.selectElement(''#id'')","b":"document.getElementById(''id'')","c":"document.queryID(''id'')","d":"document.findId(''id'')"}]',
  '{"ka":["b","b","a","a","c","b","b","b","a","b","b","a","c","d","b","c","a","a","b","b","a","b","b","b","c","b","c","b","b","c","b","a","a","c","b","a","b","a","c","b"]}',
  '["The <figure> tag specifies self-contained content, like illustrations, diagrams, photos, code listings, etc.","The <audio> element is used to embed sound content in HTML5 documents.","The <nav> tag defines a set of navigation links.","HTML stands for Hyper Text Markup Language. It is the standard markup language for creating web pages.","The W3C (World Wide Web Consortium) is the international standards organization for the World Wide Web.","<h1> defines the most important and largest heading in HTML.","The <br> tag inserts a single line break in HTML.","In modern HTML5, background color should be styled using inline CSS style attribute.","The <strong> tag is used to define text with strong importance, typically rendered in bold.","The <em> tag is used to define emphasized text, typically rendered in italic.","The id attribute specifies a unique id for an HTML element, which must be unique within the document.","The <a> element defines a hyperlink, and the href attribute specifies the URL of the page.","The alt attribute provides alternative text for images if they fail to load or for screen readers.","The input type=\"range\" defines a control for entering a number whose exact value is not important.","The <textarea> tag defines a multi-line text input control, often used for comments or feedback.","The GET method appends form data to the URL query string, making it visible and bookmarkable.","The <td> tag defines a standard data cell in an HTML table.","The colspan attribute defines the number of columns a table cell should span.","The <figure> tag specifies self-contained content, like illustrations, diagrams, photos, code listings, etc.","The <audio> element is used to embed sound content in HTML5 documents.","The <nav> tag defines a set of navigation links.","CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets. It is used to format the layout of a webpage.","The <style> tag is used to define internal CSS rules in the head section of an HTML document.","The ''''#'''' symbol targets an element with a specific id in CSS.","The :hover pseudo-class matches when the user designates an element with a pointing device.","Padding is the space between the content of an element and its border.","Margin is the outermost layer of the box model, separating the element from other elements.","position: absolute positions an element relative to its nearest positioned ancestor.","display: flex; defines a flex container and enables flexbox layout properties.","justify-content aligns flex items along the main axis (horizontal by default).","column-gap (or grid-column-gap in older specs) defines the size of the gap between columns in grid/flexbox.","Media queries (@media) allow styles to be applied based on media features like device width.",".container is a fundamental Bootstrap class that provides a responsive, fixed-width or fluid-width container.","The <script> tag is used to embed client-side JavaScript code.","let declares a block-scoped local variable, whereas var declares a function-scoped variable.","The ''''function'''' keyword is followed by the function name and parentheses to define a function in JS.","Parentheses () are used to invoke/call a declared function in JavaScript.","The push() method adds one or more elements to the end of an array and returns its new length.","A standard JS for loop declaration contains initialization, condition, and increment expressions.","document.getElementById() returns the DOM element matching the specified ID string."]',
  'published'
);

