  'css-units-mcq-questions',
  'WEB-120',
  'CSS units',
  'Global standard',
  40,
  '[{"q":"What does CSS stand for?","a":"Computer Style Sheets","b":"Cascading Style Sheets","c":"Creative Style Sheets","d":"Colorful Style Sheets"},{"q":"Which HTML tag is used to define an internal style sheet?","a":"<css>","b":"<style>","c":"<script>","d":"<stylesheet>"},{"q":"Which is the correct CSS syntax to target an element with ID ''header''?","a":".header","b":"#header","c":"header","d":"*header"},{"q":"Which CSS selector targets elements that are currently hovered by the mouse?","a":":active","b":":visited","c":":hover","d":":focus"},{"q":"Which CSS property controls the spacing inside the border of an element?","a":"margin","b":"padding","c":"border-spacing","d":"gap"},{"q":"In the CSS box model, which layer lies outside the border?","a":"padding","b":"content","c":"margin","d":"outline"},{"q":"Which CSS position value removes an element from the normal document flow and positions it relative to its closest positioned ancestor?","a":"relative","b":"absolute","c":"static","d":"fixed"},{"q":"Which CSS display value enables a flex container?","a":"display: grid;","b":"display: flex;","c":"display: block-flex;","d":"display: inline-grid;"},{"q":"Which flexbox property defines the alignment of items along the main axis?","a":"align-items","b":"align-content","c":"justify-content","d":"flex-direction"},{"q":"Which CSS property specifies the column gap size in a Grid layout?","a":"grid-column-gap","b":"column-gap","c":"gap-columns","d":"grid-gap-width"},{"q":"What is the primary CSS rule used to apply responsive styles based on screen width?","a":"@media","b":"@import","c":"@responsive","d":"@keyframes"},{"q":"What does HTML stand for? (Study Guide Question)","a":"Hyper Text Markup Language","b":"Home Tool Markup Language","c":"Hyperlinks and Text Markup Language","d":"Hyper Tool Markup Language"},{"q":"Who is making the Web standards?","a":"Mozilla","b":"Google","c":"The World Wide Web Consortium (W3C)","d":"Microsoft"},{"q":"Choose the correct HTML element for the largest heading:","a":"<h6>","b":"<h1>","c":"<heading>","d":"<head>"},{"q":"What is the correct HTML element for inserting a line break?","a":"<break>","b":"<br>","c":"<lb>","d":"<hr>"},{"q":"What is the correct HTML for adding a background color?","a":"<body bg=\"yellow\">","b":"<body style=\"background-color:yellow;\">","c":"<background>yellow</background>","d":"<body color=\"yellow\">"},{"q":"Choose the correct HTML element to define important text: (Study Guide Question)","a":"<strong>","b":"<important>","c":"<i>","d":"<b>"},{"q":"Choose the correct HTML element to define emphasized text:","a":"<i>","b":"<em>","c":"<italic>","d":"<emphasize>"},{"q":"Which attribute is used to specify a unique identifier for an HTML element?","a":"class","b":"id","c":"style","d":"name"},{"q":"What is the correct HTML for creating a hyperlink?","a":"<a href=\"http://www.mcqsolve.com\">MCQsolve</a>","b":"<a url=\"http://www.mcqsolve.com\">MCQsolve</a>","c":"<a>http://www.mcqsolve.com</a>","d":"<a name=\"http://www.mcqsolve.com\">MCQsolve</a>"},{"q":"Which HTML attribute specifies an alternate text for an image, if the image cannot be displayed?","a":"title","b":"src","c":"alt","d":"longdesc"},{"q":"Which input type defines a slider control? (Study Guide Question)","a":"search","b":"controls","c":"slider","d":"range"},{"q":"Which HTML element is used to define a multi-line input control?","a":"<input type=\"textbox\">","b":"<textarea>","c":"<input type=\"textarea\">","d":"<textbox>"},{"q":"In HTML forms, which method sends the form data as part of the URL?","a":"POST","b":"SUBMIT","c":"GET","d":"SEND"},{"q":"Which HTML tag is used to define a table cell?","a":"<td>","b":"<tr>","c":"<th>","d":"<cell>"},{"q":"How can you make a table cell span more than one column?","a":"colspan=\"2\"","b":"rowspan=\"2\"","c":"span=\"2\"","d":"colsplit=\"2\""},{"q":"Which HTML5 element is used to represent self-contained content, like photos, diagrams, or code listings? (Study Guide Question)","a":"<section>","b":"<figure>","c":"<aside>","d":"<details>"},{"q":"What is the correct HTML5 element for playing audio files?","a":"<sound>","b":"<audio>","c":"<mp3>","d":"<play>"},{"q":"Which HTML5 tag is used to define navigation links?","a":"<nav>","b":"<navigate>","c":"<menu>","d":"<links>"},{"q":"What does CSS stand for?","a":"Computer Style Sheets","b":"Cascading Style Sheets","c":"Creative Style Sheets","d":"Colorful Style Sheets"},{"q":"Which HTML tag is used to define an internal style sheet?","a":"<css>","b":"<style>","c":"<script>","d":"<stylesheet>"},{"q":"Which is the correct CSS syntax to target an element with ID ''header''? (Study Guide Question)","a":".header","b":"#header","c":"header","d":"*header"},{"q":"Which CSS selector targets elements that are currently hovered by the mouse?","a":":active","b":":visited","c":":hover","d":":focus"},{"q":"Which CSS property controls the spacing inside the border of an element?","a":"margin","b":"padding","c":"border-spacing","d":"gap"},{"q":"In the CSS box model, which layer lies outside the border?","a":"padding","b":"content","c":"margin","d":"outline"},{"q":"Which CSS position value removes an element from the normal document flow and positions it relative to its closest positioned ancestor?","a":"relative","b":"absolute","c":"static","d":"fixed"},{"q":"Which CSS display value enables a flex container? (Study Guide Question)","a":"display: grid;","b":"display: flex;","c":"display: block-flex;","d":"display: inline-grid;"},{"q":"Which flexbox property defines the alignment of items along the main axis?","a":"align-items","b":"align-content","c":"justify-content","d":"flex-direction"},{"q":"Which CSS property specifies the column gap size in a Grid layout?","a":"grid-column-gap","b":"column-gap","c":"gap-columns","d":"grid-gap-width"},{"q":"What is the primary CSS rule used to apply responsive styles based on screen width?","a":"@media","b":"@import","c":"@responsive","d":"@keyframes"}]',
  '{"ka":["b","b","b","c","b","c","b","b","c","b","a","a","c","b","b","b","a","b","b","a","c","d","b","c","a","a","b","b","a","b","b","b","c","b","c","b","b","c","b","a"]}',
  '["CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets. It is used to format the layout of a webpage.","The <style> tag is used to define internal CSS rules in the head section of an HTML document.","The ''''#'''' symbol targets an element with a specific id in CSS.","The :hover pseudo-class matches when the user designates an element with a pointing device.","Padding is the space between the content of an element and its border.","Margin is the outermost layer of the box model, separating the element from other elements.","position: absolute positions an element relative to its nearest positioned ancestor.","display: flex; defines a flex container and enables flexbox layout properties.","justify-content aligns flex items along the main axis (horizontal by default).","column-gap (or grid-column-gap in older specs) defines the size of the gap between columns in grid/flexbox.","Media queries (@media) allow styles to be applied based on media features like device width.","HTML stands for Hyper Text Markup Language. It is the standard markup language for creating web pages.","The W3C (World Wide Web Consortium) is the international standards organization for the World Wide Web.","<h1> defines the most important and largest heading in HTML.","The <br> tag inserts a single line break in HTML.","In modern HTML5, background color should be styled using inline CSS style attribute.","The <strong> tag is used to define text with strong importance, typically rendered in bold.","The <em> tag is used to define emphasized text, typically rendered in italic.","The id attribute specifies a unique id for an HTML element, which must be unique within the document.","The <a> element defines a hyperlink, and the href attribute specifies the URL of the page.","The alt attribute provides alternative text for images if they fail to load or for screen readers.","The input type=\"range\" defines a control for entering a number whose exact value is not important.","The <textarea> tag defines a multi-line text input control, often used for comments or feedback.","The GET method appends form data to the URL query string, making it visible and bookmarkable.","The <td> tag defines a standard data cell in an HTML table.","The colspan attribute defines the number of columns a table cell should span.","The <figure> tag specifies self-contained content, like illustrations, diagrams, photos, code listings, etc.","The <audio> element is used to embed sound content in HTML5 documents.","The <nav> tag defines a set of navigation links.","CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets. It is used to format the layout of a webpage.","The <style> tag is used to define internal CSS rules in the head section of an HTML document.","The ''''#'''' symbol targets an element with a specific id in CSS.","The :hover pseudo-class matches when the user designates an element with a pointing device.","Padding is the space between the content of an element and its border.","Margin is the outermost layer of the box model, separating the element from other elements.","position: absolute positions an element relative to its nearest positioned ancestor.","display: flex; defines a flex container and enables flexbox layout properties.","justify-content aligns flex items along the main axis (horizontal by default).","column-gap (or grid-column-gap in older specs) defines the size of the gap between columns in grid/flexbox.","Media queries (@media) allow styles to be applied based on media features like device width."]',
  'published'
);

