  '["HTML stands for Hyper Text Markup Language. It is the standard markup language for creating web pages.","The W3C (World Wide Web Consortium) is the international standards organization for the World Wide Web.","<h1> defines the most important and largest heading in HTML.","CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets. It is used to format the layout of a webpage.","The <style> tag is used to define internal CSS rules in the head section of an HTML document.","The <script> tag is used to embed client-side JavaScript code.","let declares a block-scoped local variable, whereas var declares a function-scoped variable.","The ''''function'''' keyword is followed by the function name and parentheses to define a function in JS.","Parentheses () are used to invoke/call a declared function in JavaScript.","The push() method adds one or more elements to the end of an array and returns its new length.","A standard JS for loop declaration contains initialization, condition, and increment expressions.","document.getElementById() returns the DOM element matching the specified ID string.","The onclick event handler triggers when an element is clicked by a pointer device.","Python source files terminate with the .py extension.","SQL stands for Structured Query Language. It is used to query databases.","The SELECT statement is used to select and retrieve data from one or more tables.","The WHERE clause filters rows that meet a boolean condition.","The OS manages hardware allocation, memory, processes, files, and provides APIs.","The CPU performs arithmetic, logical, and control operations, acting as the brain.","HTML stands for Hyper Text Markup Language. It is the standard markup language for creating web pages.","The W3C (World Wide Web Consortium) is the international standards organization for the World Wide Web.","<h1> defines the most important and largest heading in HTML.","The <br> tag inserts a single line break in HTML.","In modern HTML5, background color should be styled using inline CSS style attribute.","The <strong> tag is used to define text with strong importance, typically rendered in bold.","The <em> tag is used to define emphasized text, typically rendered in italic.","The id attribute specifies a unique id for an HTML element, which must be unique within the document.","The <a> element defines a hyperlink, and the href attribute specifies the URL of the page.","The alt attribute provides alternative text for images if they fail to load or for screen readers.","The input type=\"range\" defines a control for entering a number whose exact value is not important.","The <textarea> tag defines a multi-line text input control, often used for comments or feedback.","The GET method appends form data to the URL query string, making it visible and bookmarkable.","The <td> tag defines a standard data cell in an HTML table.","The colspan attribute defines the number of columns a table cell should span.","The <figure> tag specifies self-contained content, like illustrations, diagrams, photos, code listings, etc.","The <audio> element is used to embed sound content in HTML5 documents.","The <nav> tag defines a set of navigation links.","CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets. It is used to format the layout of a webpage.","The <style> tag is used to define internal CSS rules in the head section of an HTML document.","The ''''#'''' symbol targets an element with a specific id in CSS."]',
  'published'
);

