er of columns a table cell should span.","The <figure> tag specifies self-contained content, like illustrations, diagrams, photos, code listings, etc.","The <audio> element is used to embed sound content in HTML5 documents.","The <nav> tag defines a set of navigation links.","CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets. It is used to format the layout of a webpage.","The <style> tag is used to define internal CSS rules in the head section of an HTML document.","The ''''#'''' symbol targets an element with a specific id in CSS.","The :hover pseudo-class matches when the user designates an element with a pointing device.","Padding is the space between the content of an element and its border.","Margin is the outermost layer of the box model, separating the element from other elements.","position: absolute positions an element relative to its nearest positioned ancestor.","display: flex; defines a flex container and enables flexbox layout properties.","justify-content aligns flex items along the main axis (horizontal by default).","column-gap (or grid-column-gap in older specs) defines the size of the gap between columns in grid/flexbox.","Media queries (@media) allow styles to be applied based on media features like device width.",".container is a fundamental Bootstrap class that provides a responsive, fixed-width or fluid-width container.","The <script> tag is used to embed client-side JavaScript code.","let declares a block-scoped local variable, whereas var declares a function-scoped variable."]',
  'published'
);

