  'OS--195',
  'Computer network',
  'Global standard',
  40,
  '[{"q":"What does HTML stand for?","a":"Hyper Text Markup Language","b":"Home Tool Markup Language","c":"Hyperlinks and Text Markup Language","d":"Hyper Tool Markup Language"},{"q":"Who is making the Web standards?","a":"Mozilla","b":"Google","c":"The World Wide Web Consortium (W3C)","d":"Microsoft"},{"q":"Choose the correct HTML element for the largest heading:","a":"<h6>","b":"<h1>","c":"<heading>","d":"<head>"},{"q":"What does CSS stand for?","a":"Computer Style Sheets","b":"Cascading Style Sheets","c":"Creative Style Sheets","d":"Colorful Style Sheets"},{"q":"Which HTML tag is used to define an internal style sheet?","a":"<css>","b":"<style>","c":"<script>","d":"<stylesheet>"},{"q":"Inside which HTML element do we put JavaScript?","a":"<js>","b":"<scripting>","c":"<script>","d":"<javascript>"},{"q":"What is the correct file extension for Python files?","a":".pyt","b":".py","c":".python","d":".p"},{"q":"What does SQL stand for?","a":"Structured Query Language","b":"Simple Query Language","c":"Sequential Query Language","d":"Standard Query Language"},{"q":"Which SQL statement is used to retrieve data from a database?","a":"EXTRACT","b":"SELECT","c":"GET","d":"OPEN"},{"q":"Which SQL clause is used to filter records based on a specified condition?","a":"WHERE","b":"HAVING","c":"GROUP BY","d":"ORDER BY"},{"q":"What is the primary purpose of an Operating System?","a":"To write word documents","b":"To manage computer hardware and software resources","c":"To display web pages","d":"To prevent computer viruses"},{"q":"What OSI layer is responsible for routing data packets across networks?","a":"Physical Layer","b":"Data Link Layer","c":"Network Layer","d":"Transport Layer"},{"q":"Which protocol is used to resolve a domain name (like google.com) to an IP address?","a":"HTTP","b":"DNS","c":"FTP","d":"SMTP"},{"q":"Which TCP/IP protocol ensures reliable, ordered, error-checked delivery of a stream of packets?","a":"UDP","b":"IP","c":"TCP","d":"ICMP"},{"q":"What port number does the secure HTTPS protocol use by default?","a":"80","b":"21","c":"443","d":"8080"},{"q":"What is the brain of the computer system?","a":"RAM","b":"Hard Disk","c":"Central Processing Unit (CPU)","d":"Motherboard"},{"q":"What does HTML stand for? (Study Guide Question)","a":"Hyper Text Markup Language","b":"Home Tool Markup Language","c":"Hyperlinks and Text Markup Language","d":"Hyper Tool Markup Language"},{"q":"Who is making the Web standards?","a":"Mozilla","b":"Google","c":"The World Wide Web Consortium (W3C)","d":"Microsoft"},{"q":"Choose the correct HTML element for the largest heading:","a":"<h6>","b":"<h1>","c":"<heading>","d":"<head>"},{"q":"What is the correct HTML element for inserting a line break?","a":"<break>","b":"<br>","c":"<lb>","d":"<hr>"},{"q":"What is the correct HTML for adding a background color?","a":"<body bg=\"yellow\">","b":"<body style=\"background-color:yellow;\">","c":"<background>yellow</background>","d":"<body color=\"yellow\">"},{"q":"Choose the correct HTML element to define important text: (Study Guide Question)","a":"<strong>","b":"<important>","c":"<i>","d":"<b>"},{"q":"Choose the correct HTML element to define emphasized text:","a":"<i>","b":"<em>","c":"<italic>","d":"<emphasize>"},{"q":"Which attribute is used to specify a unique identifier for an HTML element?","a":"class","b":"id","c":"style","d":"name"},{"q":"What is the correct HTML for creating a hyperlink?","a":"<a href=\"http://www.mcqsolve.com\">MCQsolve</a>","b":"<a url=\"http://www.mcqsolve.com\">MCQsolve</a>","c":"<a>http://www.mcqsolve.com</a>","d":"<a name=\"http://www.mcqsolve.com\">MCQsolve</a>"},{"q":"Which HTML attribute specifies an alternate text for an image, if the image cannot be displayed?","a":"title","b":"src","c":"alt","d":"longdesc"},{"q":"Which input type defines a slider control? (Study Guide Question)","a":"search","b":"controls","c":"slider","d":"range"},{"q":"Which HTML element is used to define a multi-line input control?","a":"<input type=\"textbox\">","b":"<textarea>","c":"<input type=\"textarea\">","d":"<textbox>"},{"q":"In HTML forms, which method sends the form data as part of the URL?","a":"POST","b":"SUBMIT","c":"GET","d":"SEND"},{"q":"Which HTML tag is used to define a table cell?","a":"<td>","b":"<tr>","c":"<th>","d":"<cell>"},{"q":"How can you make a table cell span more than one column?","a":"colspan=\"2\"","b":"rowspan=\"2\"","c":"span=\"2\"","d":"colsplit=\"2\""},{"q":"Which HTML5 element is used to represent self-contained content, like photos, diagrams, or code listings? (Study Guide Question)","a":"<section>","b":"<figure>","c":"<aside>","d":"<details>"},{"q":"What is the correct HTML5 element for playing audio files?","a":"<sound>","b":"<audio>","c":"<mp3>","d":"<play>"},{"q":"Which HTML5 tag is used to define navigation links?","a":"<nav>","b":"<navigate>","c":"<menu>","d":"<links>"},{"q":"What does CSS stand for?","a":"Computer Style Sheets","b":"Cascading Style Sheets","c":"Creative Style Sheets","d":"Colorful Style Sheets"},{"q":"Which HTML tag is used to define an internal style sheet?","a":"<css>","b":"<style>","c":"<script>","d":"<stylesheet>"},{"q":"Which is the correct CSS syntax to target an element with ID ''header''? (Study Guide Question)","a":".header","b":"#header","c":"header","d":"*header"},{"q":"Which CSS selector targets elements that are currently hovered by the mouse?","a":":active","b":":visited","c":":hover","d":":focus"},{"q":"Which CSS property controls the spacing inside the border of an element?","a":"margin","b":"padding","c":"border-spacing","d":"gap"},{"q":"In the CSS box model, which layer lies outside the border?","a":"padding","b":"content","c":"margin","d":"outline"}]',
  '{"ka":["a","c","b","b","b","c","b","a","b","a","b","c","b","c","c","c","a","c","b","b","b","a","b","b","a","c","d","b","c","a","a","b","b","a","b","b","b","c","b","c"]}',
  '["HTML stands for Hyper Text Markup Language. It is the standard markup language for creating web pages.","The W3C (World Wide Web Consortium) is the international standards organization for the World Wide Web.","<h1> defines the most important and largest heading in HTML.","CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets. It is used to format the layout of a webpage.","The <style> tag is used to define internal CSS rules in the head section of an HTML document.","The <script> tag is used to embed client-side JavaScript code.","Python source files terminate with the .py extension.","SQL stands for Structured Query Language. It is used to query databases.","The SELECT statement is used to select and retrieve data from one or more tables.","The WHERE clause filters rows that meet a boolean condition.","The OS manages hardware allocation, memory, processes, files, and provides APIs.","The Network Layer manages logical addressing (IP) and path determination (routing).","Domain Name System (DNS) translates human-readable hostnames to numeric IP addresses.","Transmission Control Protocol (TCP) is connection-oriented and guarantees data delivery.","HTTPS default port is 443. Standard HTTP uses port 80.","The CPU performs arithmetic, logical, and control operations, acting as the brain.","HTML stands for Hyper Text Markup Language. It is the standard markup language for creating web pages.","The W3C (World Wide Web Consortium) is the international standards organization for the World Wide Web.","<h1> defines the most important and largest heading in HTML.","The <br> tag inserts a single line break in HTML.","In modern HTML5, background color should be styled using inline CSS style attribute.","The <strong> tag is used to define text with strong importance, typically rendered in bold.","The <em> tag is used to define emphasized text, typically rendered in italic.","The id attribute specifies a unique id for an HTML element, which must be unique within the document.","The <a> element defines a hyperlink, and the href attribute specifies the URL of the page.","The alt attribute provides alternative text for images if they fail to load or for screen readers.","The input type=\"range\" defines a control for entering a number whose exact value is not important.","The <textarea> tag defines a multi-line text input control, often used for comments or feedback.","The GET method appends form data to the URL query string, making it visible and bookmarkable.","The <td> tag defines a standard data cell in an HTML table.","The colspan attribute defines the number of columns a table cell should span.","The <figure> tag specifies self-contained content, like illustrations, diagrams, photos, code listings, etc.","The <audio> element is used to embed sound content in HTML5 documents.","The <nav> tag defines a set of navigation links.","CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets. It is used to format the layout of a webpage.","The <style> tag is used to define internal CSS rules in the head section of an HTML document.","The ''''#'''' symbol targets an element with a specific id in CSS.","The :hover pseudo-class matches when the user designates an element with a pointing device.","Padding is the space between the content of an element and its border.","Margin is the outermost layer of the box model, separating the element from other elements."]',
  'published'
);

