ecifies an alternate text for an image, if the image cannot be displayed?","a":"title","b":"src","c":"alt","d":"longdesc"},{"q":"Which input type defines a slider control? (Study Guide Question)","a":"search","b":"controls","c":"slider","d":"range"},{"q":"Which HTML element is used to define a multi-line input control?","a":"<input type=\"textbox\">","b":"<textarea>","c":"<input type=\"textarea\">","d":"<textbox>"},{"q":"In HTML forms, which method sends the form data as part of the URL?","a":"POST","b":"SUBMIT","c":"GET","d":"SEND"},{"q":"Which HTML tag is used to define a table cell?","a":"<td>","b":"<tr>","c":"<th>","d":"<cell>"},{"q":"How can you make a table cell span more than one column?","a":"colspan=\"2\"","b":"rowspan=\"2\"","c":"span=\"2\"","d":"colsplit=\"2\""},{"q":"Which HTML5 element is used to represent self-contained content, like photos, diagrams, or code listings? (Study Guide Question)","a":"<section>","b":"<figure>","c":"<aside>","d":"<details>"},{"q":"What is the correct HTML5 element for playing audio files?","a":"<sound>","b":"<audio>","c":"<mp3>","d":"<play>"},{"q":"Which HTML5 tag is used to define navigation links?","a":"<nav>","b":"<navigate>","c":"<menu>","d":"<links>"},{"q":"What does CSS stand for?","a":"Computer Style Sheets","b":"Cascading Style Sheets","c":"Creative Style Sheets","d":"Colorful Style Sheets"},{"q":"Which HTML tag is used to define an internal style sheet?","a":"<css>","b":"<style>","c":"<script>","d":"<stylesheet>"},{"q":"Which is the correct CSS syntax to target an element with ID ''header''? (Study Guide Question)","a":".header","b":"#header","c":"header","d":"*header"},{"q":"Which CSS selector targets elements that are currently hovered by the mouse?","a":":active","b":":visited","c":":hover","d":":focus"},{"q":"Which CSS property controls the spacing inside the border of an element?","a":"margin","b":"padding","c":"border-spacing","d":"gap"},{"q":"In the CSS box model, which layer lies outside the border?","a":"padding","b":"content","c":"margin","d":"outline"},{"q":"Which CSS position value removes an element from the normal document flow and positions it relative to its closest positioned ancestor?","a":"relative","b":"absolute","c":"static","d":"fixed"},{"q":"Which CSS display value enables a flex container? (Study Guide Question)","a":"display: grid;","b":"display: flex;","c":"display: block-flex;","d":"display: inline-grid;"},{"q":"Which flexbox property defines the alignment of items along the main axis?","a":"align-items","b":"align-content","c":"justify-content","d":"flex-direction"},{"q":"Which CSS property specifies the column gap size in a Grid layout?","a":"grid-column-gap","b":"column-gap","c":"gap-columns","d":"grid-gap-width"},{"q":"What is the primary CSS rule used to apply responsive styles based on screen width?","a":"@media","b":"@import","c":"@responsive","d":"@keyframes"},{"q":"Which Bootstrap class is used to create a responsive container?","a":".container","b":".row","c":".col-md-12","d":".grid-responsive"},{"q":"Inside which HTML element do we put JavaScript? (Study Guide Question)","a":"<js>","b":"<scripting>","c":"<script>","d":"<javascript>"},{"q":"Which keyword is used to declare a block-scoped variable in ES6?","a":"var","b":"let","c":"define","d":"set"},{"q":"How do you write a function in JavaScript?","a":"function myFunction()","b":"function:myFunction()","c":"def myFunction()","d":"create myFunction()"},{"q":"How do you call a function named ''myFunction''?","a":"call myFunction()","b":"myFunction()","c":"execute myFunction","d":"run myFunction"},{"q":"Which method adds a new element to the end of a JavaScript array?","a":"push()","b":"pop()","c":"shift()","d":"unshift()"},{"q":"How does a ''for'' loop start in JavaScript? (Study Guide Question)","a":"for (i = 0; i <= 5)","b":"for (i <= 5; i++)","c":"for (let i = 0; i <= 5; i++)","d":"for i = 1 to 5"}]',
