e.","The <style> tag is used to define internal CSS rules in the head section of an HTML document.","The ''''#'''' symbol targets an element with a specific id in CSS.","The :hover pseudo-class matches when the user designates an element with a pointing device.","Padding is the space between the content of an element and its border.","Margin is the outermost layer of the box model, separating the element from other elements.","position: absolute positions an element relative to its nearest positioned ancestor.","display: flex; defines a flex container and enables flexbox layout properties.","justify-content aligns flex items along the main axis (horizontal by default).","column-gap (or grid-column-gap in older specs) defines the size of the gap between columns in grid/flexbox.","Media queries (@media) allow styles to be applied based on media features like device width.",".container is a fundamental Bootstrap class that provides a responsive, fixed-width or fluid-width container.","The <script> tag is used to embed client-side JavaScript code.","let declares a block-scoped local variable, whereas var declares a function-scoped variable.","The ''''function'''' keyword is followed by the function name and parentheses to define a function in JS.","Parentheses () are used to invoke/call a declared function in JavaScript.","The push() method adds one or more elements to the end of an array and returns its new length.","A standard JS for loop declaration contains initialization, condition, and increment expressions."]',
